+
+**Additive native split, 2026-11-18:** `wait_for_exit(timeout)` observes the original root and Job without closing any handles or consuming admission. `ExitObservation::Pending` distinguishes a live root from an exited root with live members; `ExitObservation::Exited { root_exit }` retains the process, primary-thread and Job handles. It is not `Settlement::Complete`, a product capability, or permission to close resources. Repeating the observation uses the same owner. A call after recorded closure is rejected rather than presented as a fresh resource observation.
+
